'''Parablastoidea''' is a small class of [[blastozoan]] [[echinoderm]]s restricted to the [[Ordovician]] period ([[Floian]] to [[Katian]]).  Like all traditinal blastozoan classes, the parablastoids are distinguished by their respiratory structures, which in this group are known as ''cataspires''.  While many traditional blastozoan classes have proven [[paraphyletic]] or [[polyphyletic]], no evidence has emerged to challenge the view of this small class as [[monophyletic]].

